    "text": "Here's the implementation of the `anti_shuffle` function:\n\n\n```\ndef anti_shuffle(s):\n    # Split the string into individual words\n    words = s.split('() \n    \n    # Sort each word\n    sorted_words = [ [sorted(word)  for word for word in words]\n\n    # Join the sorted words words into a single string\n    result = ' '.join(sorted_words)\n    \n    return result\n```\n\nThis function works by first splitting the input string into individual words, sorting each word alphabetically, and then joining the sorted words back into a single string.",
